{"metadata":{"title":"InjectedObservable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"InjectedObservable"}],"platforms":[{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"17.0"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"17.0"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"17.0"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"14.0"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"17.0"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"10.0"}],"externalID":"s:10FactoryKit18InjectedObservableV","modules":[{"name":"FactoryKit"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"InjectedObservable"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A property wrapper that injects an Observable dependency into a SwiftUI view."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/InjectedObservable\/init(_:)-5387n","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/InjectedObservable\/init(_:)-8hen6","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/InjectedObservable\/init(_:)-zktg"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/InjectedObservable\/projectedValue","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/InjectedObservable\/wrappedValue"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/InjectedObservable\/DynamicProperty-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@propertyWrapper"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"InjectedObservable"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Observation10ObservableP","text":"Observable"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Scenes"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"InjectedObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is designed to automatically resolve and inject Observable dependencies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from a shared container, allowing for easy management of Observable objects within","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI views. This property wrapper ensures that the dependency is resolved on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first use and provides state storage, direct access, and binding capabilities.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"And unlike using State (prior to iOS 27), the injected dependency is only resolved once, on first use.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To use ","type":"text"},{"code":"InjectedObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" just add the view model dependency to a Factory container.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Define the dependency","extension Container {","    @MainActor var sceneDemoViewModel: Factory<SceneDemoViewModel> {","        self { SceneDemoViewModel() }","    }","}","\/\/ And use the property wrapper in the View to obtain the view model.","struct SceneDemoView: View {","    @InjectedObservable(\\.sceneDemoViewModel) var model","    var body: some View {","        Text(model.text)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"InjectedObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can also look for a registered scene container and use that container instead of Container.shared. This can be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"beneficial in multitasking environments like SplitView.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To do so, register and store the container at the scene root, NOT the app root.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@main","struct DemoApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            PerSceneContentView()","        }","    }","}","\/\/ Create a new container for each scene.","struct PerSceneContentView: View {","    @State var sceneContainer = Container()","    var body: some View {","        ContentView()","            .environment(\\.container, sceneContainer)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You’ll probably also want to pass the container into the view model on initialization so it’s accessing the proper dependencies. Using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Injected","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or other Factory property wrappers will revert to accessing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Container.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is not what we want.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["extension Container {","    @MainActor var sceneDemoViewModel: Factory<SceneDemoViewModel> {","        self { SceneDemoViewModel(container: self) }","    }","}","","@MainActor","@Observable","final class SceneDemoViewModel {","    private let service: MyServiceType","    init(container: Container) {","        \/\/ If you want the service resolved from the \"per scene\" container do this!","        self.service = container.myServiceType()","    }","    \/\/ Not this!","    @Injected(\\.myServiceType) private var badDependency","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This property wrapper is available on iOS 17.0, macOS 14.0, tvOS 17.0, and watchOS 10.0."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wrapped type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":" must conform to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Requires"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/7SwiftUI15DynamicPropertyP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/factorykit\/injectedobservable"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/InjectedObservable","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://FactoryKit/7SwiftUI15DynamicPropertyP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/7SwiftUI15DynamicPropertyP","title":"SwiftUICore.DynamicProperty"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Scenes":{"kind":"article","title":"Per-Scene Containers","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Giving every window its own container instead of sharing one global."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/scenes","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Scenes"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/InjectedObservable/wrappedValue":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/F